WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.100
I will make your wish come true.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.870
Even if it means hurting someone.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.540
Even if it means hurting myself.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.250
So please, once your wish comes true...

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.150
All I'll ask for...

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.900
...is your smile.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:13.460
shinjitsu wa hitoe ni kaado no uraomote
Truth and reality are like the two sides of a card

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.970
tokenai mama
Forever entwined

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.730
mekurimekuru meku
Thrust upon this chaotic stage

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:27.730
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:28.980
memagurushii suteeji de
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:37.030
sono karamatta kanjou wo manzoku iku made nankai mo
Until I can finally sort out these mixed-up emotions

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:40.280
kowashite shimae
I'll destroy it countless times

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:45.370
unmei ni temaneki sare samayou ashita wa
The uncertain future will be summoned by fate

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:50.670
nani wo erande nani wo tebanashi hitotsu ni nareba iin darou
Should I choose just one thing to let go of?

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:56.420
najitta tefuda wo sarasu yoyuu nante nai yo
I can't afford to let my sinful hand show yet

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.510
kawaita koukai no umi wo nomihosu hibi wa
My days of leisurely drinking from the sea of regret are long over

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:06.850
kagirareta kotoba de itsushika no egao yurushite hoshiin darou
Will you really use your one wish to return that lost smile?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:13.070
utsutsu wo wasuretatte kamawanai yo dakara
It's no concern of mine if you avert your eyes from reality

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:17.820
ima wa shiranai de itai nee
So please just live in blissful ignorance

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.410
What, really? Iona's playing WIXOSS, too?

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.840
Hey, WIXOSS is fun stuff, really! I even bought a starter deck.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.720
Yeah, but isn't this just, like, boys stuff?

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.940
Ruu-chan, welcome home!

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.900
Grandma!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.700
Kominato

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.870
I'm back, Grandma!

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.580
Long time no see, Nii-chan!

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.420
Hey, Ruuko.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.630
Grandma!

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.790
C'mon, at least put your bag away...

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:08.720
It looks like they're constructing an
apartment building. It's my win.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.440
I was so sure it'd be a office building.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.190
Now I have to clean the bath for one week...

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:20.400
But at the end of the day,
either of those is just a big pillar.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.900
A big pillar?

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.490
When the construction work is over, it'll be just like they planted a big pillar in that alley, right?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.450
A pillar...?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.330
Oh...

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.670
Yes. And with a pillar right there...

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.090
it'll feel like the city is just about to disappear.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:53.850
All right! Grandma, your
custom-made stage was pretty hard.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:56.440
My, I guess it's time for our dinner.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.980
I'll help you!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:02.400
You just came home, so relax for a while.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.280
Yeah, you just left your bag wherever, too— Ah, crap!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.990
Serves you right!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.200
That's what you get.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.750
It <i>stinks</i>! Onii-chan, take off your socks before you get in there!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.210
Have some more...

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.170
I'll catch athlete's foot all over!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.010
Grandma, I'll help you after all!

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.470
It sure is lively with your brother around...

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.640
But he's stinking the whole place up!

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:39.770
You must really love me to
walk me all the way out here.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:45.150
Wrong! It's just that there's a vending machine around here with my favorite milk tea.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:50.030
Ruuko, don't make Grandma too worried, you hear?

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:51.780
Worried?

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:56.960
Grandma told me you still haven't made friends at your new school.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.170
I don't really need any friends...

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:04.010
Well, you're a tough one, so I don't mind either way.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:07.680
But Grandma, you know... she can't stop worrying about you.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.760
Here.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.850
What's that?

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:15.560
Just take it.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:23.980
A buddy from my part-time job told me these cards are a hit with the girls now.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.530
I've seen some girls in my class play this.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:32.070
Use this to push your way right into their group of friends.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.210
I'm making Grandma worried...?

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.170
See ya!

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.150
Weren't you cold out there?

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.610
Coldy-coldy, warmy-warmy.

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.580
Um, I'm... I'm going to go study now!

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:36.510
I don't really care about making friends, but... I don't want to worry Grandma...

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:45.150
"The LRIG card is the player's avatar"... this one?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.730
Cute!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:53.660
So, "On the player's turn, you may..."

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.200
Her voice is cute, too!

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.210
Wait, what?!

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.390
Ouch...

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.100
Ruu-chan? Goodness, what happened?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.930
Grandma!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.520
Did you fall on your butt, Ruu-chan?

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.820
You... you don't hear that voice?

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:30.190
Voice?

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.910
<i>I'm the only one who can hear it?</i>

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:39.660
I-I'm fine! I'll go back to studying now!

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.500
You can take your bath first, okay?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:42.790
Ruu-chan?
You can take your bath first, okay?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.540
You can take your bath first, okay?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:46.460
It's cold, so make sure you keep yourself warm in there!

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:48.000
Right, right.
It's cold, so make sure you keep yourself warm in there!

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.430
Good night!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.670
<i>No! It's disappearing!</i>

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.720
Don't make it disappear!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:15.130
Jeez, this is all because I'm hearing that strange voice of yours!

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.760
So who are you?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:23.890
And why can a card <i>speak</i>—

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:24.810
Battle!

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:29.140
"Battle"? You mean you want to have a card battle?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.000
You can't eat, you know? You're made out of paper.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.010
The noodles will make you all wet when you try to eat.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.380
Battle!

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.890
Well, even if you say that to me...

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.690
It's a bit too hard to ask someone here.

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:18.900
Wait, their cards don't talk like you do, right? Why is that?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.030
Found you!

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:20.700
Huh?

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.290
You're a Selector, right?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:31.250
S-Selector?

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.080
Ha! Found your LRIG!

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.340
Huh? You can hear her voice?

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.300
Of course.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.220
See, I have a LRIG, too.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.640
This is Hanayo-san!

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.510
Come at me!

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:50.060
"Come at me"?

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:58.480
Nice!

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:01.530
Perfect! No one's around!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:06.950
Your card, Hanayo-san, isn't like my card at all.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:10.000
She doesn't purr like a cat but speaks normally.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:15.170
Your name was Ruuko-san, right?
So you can hear Hanayo-san's voice, too.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.590
Huh? You can't hear her?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.670
Well, I'm not a Selector after all.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:24.010
I have Yuzuki speak in place of Hanayo-san for me.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.050
"Selector"?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.260
Let me explain.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:32.730
Selectors are WIXOSS players who
strive to become the "Eternal Girl."

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.690
Huh? "Etern—"

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:37.860
If a Selector wins battles,
she can become her ideal self.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.230
And that self is what we call the "Eternal Girl."

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.860
You mean that her wishes come true?

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:44.700
Well, something like that I guess.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.160
To be more precise, this is not entirely correct.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:51.700
You <i>become</i> the person who can make the most outrageous wishes or dreams come true.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.290
You can <i>make</i> wishes come true?

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:59.710
Having your dreams and wishes fulfilled is nothing but fantasy.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:03.340
However, these cards can make it happen.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.680
For that, you need to keep winning in battles.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:13.640
Yet, not everyone has a deck featuring a LRIG with a mind of their own.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:17.270
Only the chosen girls, the Selectors, have them.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:25.320
Lately, public figures like female celebrities and athletes mentioned that they are playing WIXOSS.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:30.580
They are looking for other Selectors,
making it known that they own LRIGs, too.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.290
But don't forget this one thing.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.790
If you lose three battles, you also lose the right to be a Selector.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:40.250
The right?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.760
The moment you lose your third battle, we disappear.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.260
Your dreams won't come true,

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:50.550
and you will be barred from the world of WIXOSS and its strife to become the Eternal Girl.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:54.680
Thanks, Hanayo-san!
All right then, Ruuko, let's battle!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:58.190
B-But I don't have any wishes right now, and—

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.100
That's fine!

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:02.020
You can battle even without a wish.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:02.980
Battle!

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.900
Battle! Battle!

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:08.990
See? She wants to fight, too. One battle won't hurt.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.780
I guess you're right...

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:11.910
Great!

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:16.120
Yuzuki, isn't it too sudden to jump straight into a battle when she doesn't even know the rules yet?

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:20.290
No mercy! I'm gonna win this before she gets to know the rules!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:21.590
Open!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.870
Where... is this?

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:54.580
Um...

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.200
Battle!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.960
"Battle"?

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.880
Yuzuki-san! Hanayo-san!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.090
All right, I get to go first!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:14.720
Okay, it's your turn now, Ruuko!

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:17.770
Wh-What do you mean by "turn"?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.060
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:21.310
Kazuki!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:30.860
The rules are simple. Summon a SIGNI, call out the name of your LRIG, and then attack.

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:35.030
Hey! Kazuki! Why are you on Ruuko's side?!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.870
He can't hear your voice from the outside.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.540
<i>Call her name!</i>

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.250
Name? Um...

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.460
T-Tama.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:50.420
Why "Tama"?

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:55.390
Well, the sounds she makes reminds me of the cat Grandma and I used to own.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.560
Tama!

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:58.520
I'll give it a try!

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:03.690
Level 1, Grow! I summon a SIGNI! Tama, attack!

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.860
Tama!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:19.790
I-It's gone... It's really gone! Hey, is it okay?!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.540
Relax, this is only a game.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:24.170
The card will recover by the next battle.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.250
It'll recover? I see...

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.920
See what you've done, Kazuki?!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.630
I could've won this easily if she hadn't known the rules!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.510
<i>Yuzuki, can you hear me, too?</i>

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:37.430
<i>I don't think you've been fair at all.</i>

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.890
Aren't battles supposed to be fought fair and square?

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:46.770
<i>Even more so if you wager your feelings to grant your wishes through them.</i>

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.690
Level 3, Grow!

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.410
Battles are fun!

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.870
T-Tama?

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.330
More battles!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:12.300
Why? Why is she so strong even though she's barely started? If this keeps up...

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.760
Hey, Yuzuki! Do you want to lose here or something?!

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:16.970
Hanayo-san...

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:20.560
Get a hold of yourself! You said that you wanted to make Kazuki your own—

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:26.400
D-Don't say that out loud! Hanayo-san! <i>Hanayo-san</i>!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.060
<i>Both of you, get back!</i>

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.030
What are you kids doing?

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:42.790
Lunch is over! Hurry and get back to class!

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.200
Yes!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.500
H-Hey, wait! What about our battle?

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:54.840
If an external influence terminates the battle, the losses are not counted. It's a Non-Game.

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.930
Th-Thank goodness...

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.140
Um, about earlier...

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.350
Let's go, Kazuki!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.640
See you later!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:12.110
That... That was weird. Right, Tama?

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:15.360
Oh?

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:21.370
She's been asleep since right after the battle. So cute!

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.120
She's cute, but...

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:34.050
They use up their power in battles.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.340
They usually fall asleep when a
battle ends. Hanayo-san's the same.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.720
Yuzuki-san...?

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:46.100
Huh? Kazuki-kun isn't around?

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.190
We don't have to be together all the time just because we're twins.

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:54.150
Hey, could you keep quiet about what you heard?

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.150
What do you mean?

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.900
Stop playing dumb!

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:59.110
I-I really don't know what you mean!

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:09.540
Um, do you want to come over to my house?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.920
You're Ruu-chan's friend?

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.340
H-Hello.

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:19.050
Do you mind if we hang out?

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:20.380
Not at all.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:23.550
Right, I was going to step out for a second.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.680
Help yourself to the rice crackers.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:29.910
Man! So you <i>really</i> didn't hear me!

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.400
<b>Ruuko
Man! So you <i>really</i> didn't hear me!</b>

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:35.650
Man! So you <i>really</i> didn't hear me!

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.240
I think so...

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.950
Well, there goes all that worrying.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:47.120
The thing you didn't want me to know is your wish, right?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.040
Yeah.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.500
A wish that I want to come true.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:20:00.130
The kind of wish that can't be fulfilled just by doing your best or anything.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.840
Yuzuki-san...

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.760
Ever since I learned about WIXOSS and Hanayo-san, though,

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:09.100
I realized that things like miracles <i>can</i> happen.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.350
That's why I want to believe in it!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:14.350
The miracle of WIXOSS can turn me into an Eternal Girl,

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.190
and then I can realize another miracle.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.280
A miracle through cards...

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:24.070
In that case, let's battle again! I'll lose to you, Yuzuki-san.

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:28.030
I'm not interested in this Eternal Girl thing anyway.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:29.620
Nah, it's all right.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:35.040
I mean, it'd defeat the purpose of my wish if Kazuki ended up hating me for that...

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.630
What do you mean?

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:39.000
Never mind...

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.470
Pardon my intrusion!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:43.470
Grandma?

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:47.640
I guess young girls would prefer these over rice crackers, right?

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.100
Cake!

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:53.310
Tarts, macarons, bavarois...

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.860
Grandma, we can't possibly eat this a—

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:58.110
Thanks for the treat!

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:04.360
So good! They're really delicious! All of them are!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.370
How nice. Ruu-chan, you've found a wonderful friend.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.250
I'm recharged now. Well, see you again.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.540
Yeah, see you.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:29.260
I don't know WIXOSS too well yet, and it's a bit scary,

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:35.190
but I owe it to you for making Grandma happy.

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.020
Ruu-chan, dinner is ready!

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:44.530
Coming! Grandma, I want to show you something!

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:45.240
What's that?

